{%- comment -%}
Quota, full 800 x 480. Requires layout_version 3 from buildMergeVariables.
No legacy fallback: an older payload shows a waiting message rather than a wrong board,
because an absent window must never read as 100 % left.
One column per reported provider, one horizontal bar per quota window: the weekly windows
(including Claude's per-model `Week · Fable` and Codex's reserve) get the large treatment,
the rolling session sits underneath in small type.
Starts at the layout class: TRMNL adds the view wrapper itself and its markup linter
rejects a hand-written `view view--full` (checked against the live API, 2026-09-15).
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign data = merge_variables -%}
{%- comment -%}
A webhook payload reaches the template with its merge variables at the root on some TRMNL
versions and under `merge_variables` on others, so every read tries both. `default:` is
safe here because both sources carry the same value: falling through never changes it.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign version = layout_version | default: data.layout_version -%}
{%- assign ids = 'claude,codex,gemini' | split: ',' -%}
{%- assign word = display_word | default: data.display_word | default: 'left' -%}
{%- assign updated_at = updated | default: data.updated | default: '--:--' -%}
{%- comment -%}
Which account this screen is about, taken from the plugin instance's name: two instances of
this same markup, "Quota Perso" and "Quota Pro", fed by two collectors, tell two accounts
apart with nothing to configure in the relay, and the label shows even before the first
payload arrives. A plugin named plain "Quota" gets no banner.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign account = trmnl.plugin_settings.instance_name | default: '' | remove_first: 'Quota' | strip | upcase -%}
<div class="layout" style="flex-direction: column; align-items: stretch; justify-content: flex-start; padding: 10px 14px 0 14px; background: white; color: black; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;">
  {% if account != blank %}
  {%- comment -%}
  An SVG outline, like the bars: a CSS border can be dropped on the way to the screen. Black
  type on white, not a filled band: a solid black band outweighed the numbers it labels.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <svg role="img" aria-label="{{ account | escape }} account" width="100%" height="40" style="display: block; flex: 0 0 auto; margin-bottom: 10px;">
    <rect x="0" y="0" width="100%" height="100%" fill="white" stroke="black" stroke-width="4"/>
    <text x="14" y="30" fill="black" font-family="Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" font-size="30" font-weight="700" letter-spacing="3">{{ account | escape }}</text>
    <text x="100%" dx="-14" y="26" text-anchor="end" fill="black" font-family="Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" font-size="15" font-weight="700" letter-spacing="2">QUOTA</text>
  </svg>
  {% endif %}
  {% if version == 3 %}
  <div style="display: flex; width: 100%; align-items: flex-start; gap: 18px;">
    {%- assign reported_count = 0 -%}
    {% for id in ids %}
      {%- case id -%}
      {%- when 'claude' -%}
        {%- assign present = claude_present | default: data.claude_present -%}
        {%- assign plan = claude_plan | default: data.claude_plan -%}
        {%- assign windows = claude_windows | default: data.claude_windows -%}
      {%- when 'codex' -%}
        {%- assign present = codex_present | default: data.codex_present -%}
        {%- assign plan = codex_plan | default: data.codex_plan -%}
        {%- assign windows = codex_windows | default: data.codex_windows -%}
      {%- when 'gemini' -%}
        {%- assign present = gemini_present | default: data.gemini_present -%}
        {%- assign plan = gemini_plan | default: data.gemini_plan -%}
        {%- assign windows = gemini_windows | default: data.gemini_windows -%}
      {%- endcase -%}
      {% if present == true %}
        {%- assign reported_count = reported_count | plus: 1 -%}
        <div style="flex: 1; min-width: 0;">
          <div style="display: flex; align-items: baseline; justify-content: space-between; gap: 8px; border-bottom: 3px solid black; padding-bottom: 4px; margin-bottom: 8px;">
            <div style="font-size: 26px; font-weight: 700; line-height: 1.1;"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" aria-hidden="true">{% case id %}{% when 'claude' %}<path fill="black" d="m4.7144 15.9555 4.7174-2.6471.079-.2307-.079-.1275h-.2307l-.7893-.0486-2.6956-.0729-2.3375-.0971-2.2646-.1214-.5707-.1215-.5343-.7042.0546-.3522.4797-.3218.686.0608 1.5179.1032 2.2767.1578 1.6514.0972 2.4468.255h.3886l.0546-.1579-.1336-.0971-.1032-.0972L6.973 9.8356l-2.55-1.6879-1.3356-.9714-.7225-.4918-.3643-.4614-.1578-1.0078.6557-.7225.8803.0607.2246.0607.8925.686 1.9064 1.4754 2.4893 1.8336.3643.3035.1457-.1032.0182-.0728-.164-.2733-1.3539-2.4467-1.445-2.4893-.6435-1.032-.17-.6194c-.0607-.255-.1032-.4674-.1032-.7285L6.287.1335 6.6997 0l.9957.1336.419.3642.6192 1.4147 1.0018 2.2282 1.5543 3.0296.4553.8985.2429.8318.091.255h.1579v-.1457l.1275-1.706.2368-2.0947.2307-2.6957.0789-.7589.3764-.9107.7468-.4918.5828.2793.4797.686-.0668.4433-.2853 1.8517-.5586 2.9021-.3643 1.9429h.2125l.2429-.2429.9835-1.3053 1.6514-2.0643.7286-.8196.85-.9046.5464-.4311h1.0321l.759 1.1293-.34 1.1657-1.0625 1.3478-.8804 1.1414-1.2628 1.7-.7893 1.36.0729.1093.1882-.0183 2.8535-.607 1.5421-.2794 1.8396-.3157.8318.3886.091.3946-.3278.8075-1.967.4857-2.3072.4614-3.4364.8136-.0425.0304.0486.0607 1.5482.1457.6618.0364h1.621l3.0175.2247.7892.522.4736.6376-.079.4857-1.2142.6193-1.6393-.3886-3.825-.9107-1.3113-.3279h-.1822v.1093l1.0929 1.0686 2.0035 1.8092 2.5075 2.3314.1275.5768-.3218.4554-.34-.0486-2.2039-1.6575-.85-.7468-1.9246-1.621h-.1275v.17l.4432.6496 2.3436 3.5214.1214 1.0807-.17.3521-.6071.2125-.6679-.1214-1.3721-1.9246L14.38 17.959l-1.1414-1.9428-.1397.079-.674 7.2552-.3156.3703-.7286.2793-.6071-.4614-.3218-.7468.3218-1.4753.3886-1.9246.3157-1.53.2853-1.9004.17-.6314-.0121-.0425-.1397.0182-1.4328 1.9672-2.1796 2.9446-1.7243 1.8456-.4128.164-.7164-.3704.0667-.6618.4008-.5889 2.386-3.0357 1.4389-1.882.929-1.0868-.0062-.1579h-.0546l-6.3385 4.1164-1.1293.1457-.4857-.4554.0608-.7467.2307-.2429 1.9064-1.3114Z"/>{% when 'codex' %}<path fill="black" d="M22.2819 9.8211a5.9847 5.9847 0 0 0-.5157-4.9108 6.0462 6.0462 0 0 0-6.5098-2.9A6.0651 6.0651 0 0 0 4.9807 4.1818a5.9847 5.9847 0 0 0-3.9977 2.9 6.0462 6.0462 0 0 0 .7427 7.0966 5.98 5.98 0 0 0 .511 4.9107 6.051 6.051 0 0 0 6.5146 2.9001A5.9847 5.9847 0 0 0 13.2599 24a6.0557 6.0557 0 0 0 5.7718-4.2058 5.9894 5.9894 0 0 0 3.9977-2.9001 6.0557 6.0557 0 0 0-.7475-7.0729zm-9.022 12.6081a4.4755 4.4755 0 0 1-2.8764-1.0408l.1419-.0804 4.7783-2.7582a.7948.7948 0 0 0 .3927-.6813v-6.7369l2.02 1.1686a.071.071 0 0 1 .038.052v5.5826a4.504 4.504 0 0 1-4.4945 4.4944zm-9.6607-4.1254a4.4708 4.4708 0 0 1-.5346-3.0137l.142.0852 4.783 2.7582a.7712.7712 0 0 0 .7806 0l5.8428-3.3685v2.3324a.0804.0804 0 0 1-.0332.0615L9.74 19.9502a4.4992 4.4992 0 0 1-6.1408-1.6464zM2.3408 7.8956a4.485 4.485 0 0 1 2.3655-1.9728V11.6a.7664.7664 0 0 0 .3879.6765l5.8144 3.3543-2.0201 1.1685a.0757.0757 0 0 1-.071 0l-4.8303-2.7865A4.504 4.504 0 0 1 2.3408 7.872zm16.5963 3.8558L13.1038 8.364 15.1192 7.2a.0757.0757 0 0 1 .071 0l4.8303 2.7913a4.4944 4.4944 0 0 1-.6765 8.1042v-5.6772a.79.79 0 0 0-.407-.667zm2.0107-3.0231l-.142-.0852-4.7735-2.7818a.7759.7759 0 0 0-.7854 0L9.409 9.2297V6.8974a.0662.0662 0 0 1 .0284-.0615l4.8303-2.7866a4.4992 4.4992 0 0 1 6.6802 4.66zM8.3065 12.863l-2.02-1.1638a.0804.0804 0 0 1-.038-.0567V6.0742a4.4992 4.4992 0 0 1 7.3757-3.4537l-.142.0805L8.704 5.459a.7948.7948 0 0 0-.3927.6813zm1.0976-2.3654l2.602-1.4998 2.6069 1.4998v2.9994l-2.5974 1.4997-2.6067-1.4997Z"/>{% when 'gemini' %}<path fill="black" d="M20.616 10.835a14.147 14.147 0 01-4.45-3.001 14.111 14.111 0 01-3.678-6.452.503.503 0 00-.975 0 14.134 14.134 0 01-3.679 6.452 14.155 14.155 0 01-4.45 3.001c-.65.28-1.318.505-2.002.678a.502.502 0 000 .975c.684.172 1.35.397 2.002.677a14.147 14.147 0 014.45 3.001 14.112 14.112 0 013.679 6.453.502.502 0 00.975 0c.172-.685.397-1.351.677-2.003a14.145 14.145 0 013.001-4.45 14.113 14.113 0 016.453-3.678.503.503 0 000-.975 13.245 13.245 0 01-2.003-.678z"/>{% endcase %}</svg> {{ id | capitalize }}</div>
            <div style="font-size: 14px; text-align: right; min-width: 0; overflow-wrap: anywhere;">{{ plan | escape }}</div>
          </div>
          {% if windows == blank %}
            <div style="font-size: 30px; margin-top: 30px;">&mdash;</div>
            <div style="font-size: 16px;">No data</div>
          {% else %}
            {% for w in windows %}
              {%- comment -%}
              Inverted for critical, boxed for warn, dashed and unfilled when the reading is
              out of date: three states a 1-bit screen can tell apart at a metre, with no
              dithered grey anywhere.
              {%- endcomment -%}
              {%- if w.state == 'critical' -%}
                {%- assign ink = 'white' -%}{%- assign paper = 'black' -%}
                {%- assign box = 'background: black; color: white; padding: 5px 7px;' -%}
              {%- elsif w.state == 'warn' -%}
                {%- assign ink = 'black' -%}{%- assign paper = 'white' -%}
                {%- assign box = 'border: 2px solid black; padding: 3px 5px;' -%}
              {%- else -%}
                {%- assign ink = 'black' -%}{%- assign paper = 'white' -%}
                {%- assign box = 'padding: 0 7px 0 0;' -%}
              {%- endif -%}
              {%- if w.weekly -%}
                {%- assign label_size = 22 -%}{%- assign value_size = 30 -%}
                {%- assign bar_height = 22 -%}{%- assign reset_size = 15 -%}
                {%- assign gap = 14 -%}
              {%- else -%}
                {%- assign label_size = 16 -%}{%- assign value_size = 20 -%}
                {%- assign bar_height = 12 -%}{%- assign reset_size = 13 -%}
                {%- assign gap = 12 -%}
              {%- endif -%}
              <div style="margin-bottom: {{ gap }}px; {{ box }}">
                <div style="display: flex; align-items: baseline; justify-content: space-between; gap: 6px;">
                  <span style="font-size: {{ label_size }}px; font-weight: 600; flex: 1 1 auto; min-width: 0; overflow-wrap: anywhere;">{{ w.label | escape }}</span>
                  <span style="font-size: {{ value_size }}px; font-weight: 700; flex: 0 0 auto; white-space: nowrap;">{{ w.value }}% {{ word | escape }}</span>
                </div>
                {%- comment -%}
                SVG rectangles rather than CSS backgrounds: the device pipeline keeps vector
                fills where a background-color can be dropped, and a 1-bit screen has no
                grey to lose here. The stroke is drawn at 4px so 2px survive the edge clip.
                {%- endcomment -%}
                <svg role="img" aria-label="{{ w.label | escape }} {{ w.value }} percent {{ word | escape }}; {{ w.state_label | escape }}"
                     width="100%" height="{{ bar_height }}" style="display: block; margin-top: 3px;">
                  <rect x="0" y="0" width="100%" height="100%" fill="{{ paper }}" stroke="{{ ink }}" stroke-width="4"{% if w.state == 'stale' %} stroke-dasharray="8 5"{% endif %}/>
                  {% unless w.state == 'stale' %}<rect x="0" y="0" width="{{ w.value }}%" height="100%" fill="{{ ink }}"/>{% endunless %}
                </svg>
                <div style="font-size: {{ reset_size }}px; margin-top: 2px;">{% if w.state == 'stale' %}{{ w.state_label | escape }} &middot; {% endif %}{{ w.reset | escape }}</div>
              </div>
            {% endfor %}
          {% endif %}
        </div>
      {% endif %}
    {% endfor %}
    {% if reported_count == 0 %}<div style="font-size: 24px;">No data</div>{% endif %}
  </div>
  {% else %}
    <div style="font-size: 30px; font-weight: 700; margin-top: 36px;">Waiting for data</div>
    <div style="font-size: 18px; margin-top: 8px;">No snapshot yet from the collector on this account's Mac.</div>
  {% endif %}
</div>
<div class="title_bar" style="color: black; background: white;">
  <span class="title">Quota{% if account != blank %} &middot; {{ account | escape }}{% endif %}</span>
  <span class="instance">Updated {{ updated_at | escape }} UTC</span>
</div>
